ApiErrorCode.description:
The `code` of every /api/v1 refusal that is not a model or provider failure (those carry a StepError code), from services/apiErrors.js. Stable: the sentence may change, the code does not. Status and OpenAI type for each:
- the key and its account (authenticateApp): missing_api_key 401, invalid_api_key 401, api_key_revoked 401, api_key_expired 401, app_key_not_accepted 401 (an app_… key where only secret keys are accepted) — authentication_error; app_not_active 403, api_not_enabled 403, developer_account_not_found 403, developer_not_approved 403, user_not_found 403, account_suspended 403 — permission_error;
- policy, one per rule that refused (services/guardrailService.js): model_required 400 (invalid_request_error, param `model`); model_not_allowed 403 (the key's own model list), model_blocked_by_policy 403 (the organization's or key's model or provider policy), category_not_allowed 403, food_api_not_enabled 403, per_call_limit_exceeded 403 (the key's per-call credit ceiling), ip_not_allowed 403, tool_not_allowed 403 — permission_error; content_filtered 422 (the key's content policy) — invalid_request_error, as the contract's own 422 content_policy; rate_limit_exceeded 429 (the key's hourly request limit), daily_cost_cap_exceeded 429, budget_exhausted 429 (a key, organization or platform credit budget) — rate_limit_error, retryable, with Retry-After and X-Curvet-Limit-*;
- the routes' own: workflow_not_found 404, workflow_run_not_found 404, job_not_found 404, workflow_run_stopped 409 (someone stopped the run) — invalid_request_error; workflow_access_denied 403, workflow_run_access_denied 403 — permission_error;
- the chat routes' own request checks (POST /chat/completions, POST /playground/chat): messages_required 400 (param `messages`), invalid_parameter 400 (a request field out of range or of the wrong shape; `param` names it), model_unknown 400 (param `model`), model_not_chat 400 (param `model`), image_input_not_supported 400 (param `messages`) — invalid_request_error; balance_held 429 (a call billed per token while calls in progress hold the rest of the balance) — rate_limit_error, retryable, with Retry-After;
- the image and media routes' own request checks (POST /playground/image, /video, /audio, /3d): prompt_required 400 (param `prompt`), model_unknown (as on the chat routes), model_wrong_type 400 (a model of another kind, param `model`), text_too_long 400 (/audio, param `prompt`), upload_too_large 413 — invalid_request_error; a short balance there is the StepError code insufficient_credits (402, with `required` and `available`), and a 3D prompt over the model's limit keeps its code PROMPT_TOO_LONG (400);
- codes that shipped before this list, sent exactly as before: model_not_found 404 and insufficient_quota 402 (OpenAI's own names, on the OpenAI-style routes; type insufficient_quota for the latter); a custom model's state on the chat routes, turned_off 409 and not_ready 409 (param `model`); the Idempotency-Key refusals idempotency_key_invalid 400, idempotency_key_mismatch 422, idempotency_key_in_use 409 (retryable, with Retry-After) and idempotency_key_not_replayable 409 — invalid_request_error; PROMPT_TOO_LONG 400 (a 3D prompt over the model's limit, upper case as it shipped);
- the server itself, for a request under /api/v1: route_not_found 404, invalid_json 400, body_too_large 413, bad_request 400 (a body the parser refused for another reason, at the parser's own status: an unsupported encoding is 415) — invalid_request_error; ip_rate_limited 429 — rate_limit_error, retryable, with Retry-After. Another 4xx passed to the server's error handler keeps its status and its own sentence under the code that fits: bad_request 400, unauthorized 401 (authentication_error), forbidden 403 (permission_error), not_found 404, conflict 409, too_many_requests 429 (rate_limit_error, retryable), request_refused (any other 4xx; type by its status).
A failure on Curvet's side that is none of these is the StepError code `unknown` (500, retryable).

OpenAIErrorResponse.description:
Every error on the OpenAI-style routes (routes/api/openai.js), and the server's own answers for a request on those paths, in OpenAI's envelope. `retryable` and `request_id` are on every one. Four builders write it:
- the route's own refusals (oaError): `code` (such as `model_not_found`, `insufficient_quota`, `model_required`, `invalid_parameter`, `input_too_long`, `unknown`), `param` (the field the refusal is about, when it is about one);
- auth, policy and limit refusals ({success:false,error,code} rewritten by openAiCompat, services/apiErrors.js openAiFromNative): `code` an ApiErrorCode, `type` by it (a bad or missing key authentication_error, a permission or policy refusal permission_error, a limit rate_limit_error), `param` `model` on model_required, and on a 429 the limit in `limit`;
- a model or provider failure (stepErrors.sendOpenAiError): `code` is a StepError code and `provider`, `model`, `provider_status` are present too (null when unknown);
- an Idempotency-Key refusal (middleware/idempotency.js): `type` invalid_request_error, `code` one of the idempotency_key_* codes;
- the server itself (services/apiErrors.js): route_not_found, invalid_json, body_too_large, bad_request, unknown, ip_rate_limited.

PlaygroundErrorResponse.description:
Every error on the /api/v1/playground routes (routes/api/playground.js), and the server's own answers for a request under /api/v1 outside the OpenAI-style paths. `success` is false and `error` is always a string sentence. What else is present depends on who refused:
- auth, policy, the routes' own lookups and the server itself (services/apiErrors.js): `code` (an ApiErrorCode, or `unknown` for a failure on Curvet's side), `type`, `retryable`, and `requestId` once the API router has seen the request;
- a rate limit, daily cost cap or budget (429): also `rateLimitInfo`, `costCapInfo` or `budgetInfo`, with Retry-After and X-Curvet-Limit-* headers;
- too little balance (402) on chat, image and media: `required` (USD) and `available` (USD), plus `requiredCredits` on /audio; and `code` insufficient_credits;
- a model, provider, job or workflow-run failure (stepErrors.sendApiError): `code` (a StepError code), `type`, `retryable`, `stepError`, `requestId` (when the request log is on); `jobId` when a media job failed or polling its provider failed (GET /jobs/{jobId}), `runId` when a workflow run stopped after it was created;
- an Idempotency-Key refusal: `code` (idempotency_key_*), `type` invalid_request_error, `retryable`;
- the image and media routes' own checks: an ApiErrorCode (prompt_required, model_unknown, model_wrong_type, text_too_long, upload_too_large), or PROMPT_TOO_LONG with `message`, `promptLength` and `maxPromptLength` on a 3D prompt over the model's limit; a custom model's state code (turned_off, not_ready) on the chat route's 409;
- the server itself (a body that does not parse or is too large, a path no router serves, the per-IP rate limit): the codes above, plus the `message` it always carried, and `retryAfter` on ip_rate_limited.
